1
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:10,600
Cinderella

2
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:20,000
Cinderella's Sister

3
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:42,300
Did something happen?

4
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,600
What's wrong?

5
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:50,400
What is it?

6
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:52,700
Can you...

7
00:01:55,010 --> 00:02:00,570
take me and run away somewhere?

8
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:05,800
It's okay if I can't be forgiven.

9
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:11,400
No, I won't accept any forgiveness.

10
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:15,110
So...let's run away.

11
00:02:15,110 --> 00:02:17,700
Run away with me.

12
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,300
Let's run away!

13
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:26,600
Episode 12

14
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:14,300
If the Earth were square, I'd really try running away.

15
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:18,280
Why does it have to be round?

16
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:21,000
This sucks.

17
00:03:21,630 --> 00:03:26,440
No matter where you run, you'll end up back home.

18
00:03:35,990 --> 00:03:40,320
Don't say anything like that again.

19
00:03:42,550 --> 00:03:44,320
Let's run away?

20
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:46,800
Sure, let's go.

21
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:48,800
Let's run away.

22
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:53,600
Let's run to the end of the world and hide somewhere no one knows.

23
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:57,000
What would you do if I had said that?

24
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:01,920
Would you really go with me

25
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:06,400
if I agreed?

26
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:12,400
If you're suffering so much, what can I do?

27
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:15,700
You just stay still.

28
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:21,600
Do only what you want to do. If you want to bow down to
Hyo Seon's toenails, go ahead and do it.

29
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:24,800
If you don't want to do that, then force her to the wall as you did before,

30
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:27,800
blame her and pressure her.

31
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:30,000
Do that.

32
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:36,300
Just do what you want to do. I'll take care of everything else.

33
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,910
I...

34
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:46,200
I know what my heart is thinking very well,

35
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:50,600
but why are you like this?

36
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,400
What did you do wrong

37
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,500
for you to do so much for this family?

38
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,600
Is there something you have your eyes on?

39
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,500
Just like my mother?

40
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:17,000
There's something I need to repent for.

41
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:24,700
If I don't, I feel like I'll be like Dracula, not being able to die no matter how hard I try,

42
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:30,400
and having to live for thousands of years.

43
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:34,800
What did you do?

44
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:39,900
I...

45
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,000
can't tell you.

46
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:49,890
What if...

47
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:57,200
I run away by myself?

48
00:05:57,980 --> 00:06:00,760
If that's what you want to do, then do it.

49
00:06:02,990 --> 00:06:06,020
If you want to run away by yourself,

50
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:11,000
I'll do all I can to help you.

51
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:16,800
Where do you want to go?

52
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:07,800
No. Don't ask me to stay.

53
00:07:08,950 --> 00:07:11,750
Things would've been better if you had just let me leave.

54
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:17,700
Things would not have turned out this way.

55
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:23,000
Please forgive me.

56
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:29,600
No matter what I do, you'll forgive me anyway.

57
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:37,470
I'm tired of apologizing now.

58
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:57,800
I'll take you where you want to go. Get in.

59
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:59,000
I knew this would happen.

60
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:25,200
You're here.

61
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:28,600
I didn't know how much we have to make, so I was going to ask you.

62
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:31,600
We've made the same amount as we usually did.

63
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:35,800
We didn't want to wake you just to ask you.

64
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:46,600
Little President has come out? You came out early.

65
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:51,000
What's wrong? Does that sound weird?

66
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,800
We need a title to call you by,

67
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:57,900
but since you're so young, calling you "president" seems a bit weird.

68
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,500
Little President, are you done preparing for the prayer ritual?

69
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:08,500
The taste of the yeast will change depending on how the ritual is carried out.

70
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:10,600
We'll only trust in you, Little President.

71
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:14,400
It's great weather for making yeast today, isn't it?

72
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:16,200
- Do you think so?
- It's so beautiful today.

73
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:19,200
- Of course.
- I have a feeling the best yeast will be prepared today!

74
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:21,000
Of course!

75
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:24,900
Let's get a move on.

76
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:28,200
Step on it harder!

77
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:31,000
I'm already stepping on it hard!

78
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:40,400
♫ I am living day after day  ♫

79
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:49,400
♫ In your name when tears appear, ah  ♫

80
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:57,000
♫ I can't bear it, so I can't laugh ♫

81
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:06,000
♫ I'll call out your name again  ♫

82
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:36,000
Why aren't you wearing any gloves?

83
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:40,400
Eat something, kiddo. Why are you working so hard?

84
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:42,700
Enjoy your food.

85
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:50,400
The business at Noona's winery is so slow that at least I should work really hard, Ahjussi.

86
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:54,400
If things go just a bit wrong, my Noona Eun Jo will go hungry.

87
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,200
Hello.

88
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:08,900
Have a seat.

89
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:12,200
Why did you ask to meet me?

90
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:13,800
Do you remember me?

91
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:16,600
No, how would I remember?

92
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:20,000
You said you work for Hyo Seon's family.

93
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,600
I guess you're more than that. What do you want from me?

94
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:26,500
There is a good topic for in-depth reporting. I wanted to tell you.

95
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:39,800
So what if you write the article?

96
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:43,200
Since the piece you wrote and submitted didn't draw enough attention.

97
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:45,500
You said it didn't draw enough attention?

98
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:49,800
Yes. You know, business newspapers do not have wide circulation.

99
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:53,000
- That's not the case for online.
- Online?

100
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:57,000
There is some reaction. Not so much because of Dae Seong True Winemakers,

101
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:01,200
but people remembering the "Trash Dumpling Scandal" first started to show some response.

102
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:06,800
So people's attention is directed more to the Trash Dumpling Scandal than to Dae Seong True Winemakers.

103
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:11,400
So my company is also planning a series on reviewing the Trash Dumpling Scandal.

104
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:18,200
Right. That's a good thing too, Dong Soo.

105
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:21,200
Can't you look into writing about Dae Seong True Winemakers too?

106
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:24,800
Since your father works at Dae Seong True Winemakers.

107
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:27,200
- I have something I'm curious about.
- Go ahead and ask me.

108
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:30,600
Has it been revealed who created the adulterated supply of rice wine?

109
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:35,600
Yes. He's been sentenced to probation and received a penalty fine.

110
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:25,000
Blue Lord of the East...

111
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:29,800
Red Lord of the South...

112
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:34,000
White Lord of the West...

113
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:37,800
Black Lord of the North...

114
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:43,400
May 6 in the year of the Black Horse (2002), I invoke the guardian gods of the five directions and five earths.

115
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:46,200
I, owner of Gu Dae Seong True Winemaker, Goo Eun Jo

116
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:48,690
respectfully ask the territorial gods (5 direction gods)

117
00:14:48,730 --> 00:14:51,800
that I shall be making several hundreds, thousands of batches of leavening.

118
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:55,400
The path is pressed vertically and horizontally forming a border

119
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:59,600
and each of the five gods is arranged on the periphery.

120
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:02,600
We bow as we offer up this wine.

121
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:07,800
May you bestow divine blessings and oversee all our wishes.

122
00:15:19,770 --> 00:15:21,200
21s Current affairs
Trainee Reporter Kim Dong So

123
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:23,200
I'm a trainee reporter here.

124
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:26,800
I saw that you contributed a piece to another magazine and not ours.

125
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:29,200
Your submission seems to have raised some interest.

126
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:32,600
Dong Soo's Chief Editor asked him to cover your story separately.

127
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:35,000
Shall we start the interview?

128
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,600
Where do you want to do it? Should we do it here?

129
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:41,800
Sure. Hold on, let me call over the photographer.

130
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:14,400
You really thought Hyo Seon's dad didn't know?

131
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:16,200
He knew everything.

132
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:21,000
Even though he knew, he still loved you, Mom.

133
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,600
You wouldn't be able to complain even if you were dropped into hell.

134
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:28,100
He loved you. Hyo Seon's dad did.

135
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:56,400
Mom. The sacrificial rice cakes, offered to the spirits at the ritual, are supposed to be shared and eaten by everyone.

136
00:16:56,400 --> 00:17:00,000
Mom, you also must eat some of it.

137
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,600
Let's eat it together, Mom..

138
00:17:06,910 --> 00:17:13,400
Just like Hyo Seon's dad, she also said that it's fine with her if you don't like her.

139
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:17,600
Because she likes you, she said nothing else bothers her.

140
00:17:17,600 --> 00:17:21,000
Mom. Where you can find a father like that?

141
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Where you can find a daughter like that, Mom?

142
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,600
Where else in the world can you find people like them?!

143
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:32,010
They're delicious. The rice cakes turned out especially delicious this time.

144
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:37,030
Since we must share and eat them with everyone without making any exceptions.

145
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:43,500
Let's eat them while they're warm, Mom. I didn't eat any yet either.

146
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:46,590
I told you to stop pestering me.

147
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:14,500
Mom. They're not just regular rice cakes, they're sacrificial rice cakes offered to the spirits at the ritual.

148
00:18:14,500 --> 00:18:20,200
We're supposed to share and eat them with everyone who have good wishes for the company.

149
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:23,600
What do you think you're doing?

150
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:27,800
Are you making fun of me? Do I seem that easy to you?

151
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:30,200
Didn't you understand me telling you to leave me alone?

152
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:34,000
Why do you keep being a brown noser? Who's going to take a liking to you here?

153
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:52,300
Mom, you shouldn't act that way with food.

154
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:05,100
Are you going to make rice? I'll do it..

155
00:19:06,800 --> 00:19:08,400
Are you going to make soup?

156
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:13,500
Then you make the soup and I'll cook the rice.

157
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:17,800
Where's the rice?

158
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:19,800
You do it all then!

159
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:23,240
You do it all.

160
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:27,200
Make the rice, make the soup and get the vegetables seasoned too.

161
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,200
Okay, Mom.

162
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:35,100
I can't guarantee the taste, but I'll cook everything.

163
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:38,000
Then, you go in and get some sleep.

164
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:43,000
And... You must eat some rice cakes.

165
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,000
You understand, right?

166
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:18,900
She is such a sly fox.

167
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:23,800
She's been acting all innocent at first, but turns out to be such a large vixen..

168
00:20:28,600 --> 00:20:32,400
And so, the vegetables have been completely over-boiled.

169
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:34,800
How are you supposed to boil vegetables?

170
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:38,600
You know that I boil them really well, for as long as I could.

171
00:20:38,600 --> 00:20:43,600
You're supposed to blanch vegetables slightly, not boil them completely.

172
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:47,600
What's the difference between blanching and boiling?

173
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,200
This won't do. I'll go ahead and do it.

174
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:55,400
No, Grandma. I'll do it.

175
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:59,400
You've never tried cooking anything before, not even ramyon of all things possible.

176
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:02,700
How do you think you're going to make seasoned vegetables? They're seasoned vegetables after all!

177
00:21:02,700 --> 00:21:05,600
Excuse me. There are still some seasoned vegetables left after the ritual.

178
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:08,100
Can't she just take some and eat them for now?

179
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:11,800
There are seasoned vegetables? There are some left, Ahjumma?

180
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:20,200
Ahjumma, thank you. Grandmother, thank you.

181
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:37,500
Hyo Seon is back.

182
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,600
Mom..

183
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:59,100
What are those?

184
00:22:04,200 --> 00:22:07,200
The vegetables from earlier turned into a grass mix,

185
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:11,200
I went to go ask Grandma how to cook them,

186
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:15,800
but Ahjumma said that there were some left from the ritual.

187
00:22:15,800 --> 00:22:19,000
Grandma? Ahjumma?

188
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:27,800
I'm definitely sure I sent them away.

189
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:30,700
So, what Grandma and Ahjumma are you talking about?

190
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:36,000
There aren't many people left working in the winery...

191
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:38,000
So, Eun Jo...

192
00:22:38,800 --> 00:22:42,000
No, Unni...

193
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:47,400
I asked you to season the namool (boiled vegetable) but you didn't want to do it.

194
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:49,800
So you were going to put that on the table and say that you made it?

195
00:22:49,800 --> 00:22:52,200
No, Mom. That's not it.

196
00:22:52,200 --> 00:22:56,600
And you bring back the people that I sent out?

197
00:22:56,600 --> 00:22:59,400
That's not it! I didn't-

198
00:22:59,400 --> 00:23:02,000
And, you used Eun Jo as an excuse for it!

199
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:05,200
No, Mom.

200
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:07,600
It's not as an excuse...

201
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:10,600
You... Shut up.

202
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:17,000
Don't even say a word because I feel like fainting
just at the sound of your voice.

203
00:23:27,600 --> 00:23:29,500
Mom.

204
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:41,800
Mom! Mom!

205
00:23:44,400 --> 00:23:46,000
Mom...

206
00:23:47,600 --> 00:23:51,400
Let go of me! Where are they hiding?

207
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:00,600
Do you clearly deceive a person like this??

208
00:24:00,600 --> 00:24:03,200
Is it okay to trick someone like this?

209
00:24:03,230 --> 00:24:05,140
What on earth did you think I meant when I told you to get out of here?

210
00:24:05,150 --> 00:24:08,750
When someone tells you to get out of their house, don't you know what that means?!

211
00:24:10,600 --> 00:24:15,000
Mom. Back then, all the ahjussies stopped working and quit.

212
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:18,000
The winery was really in desperate need of workers.

213
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:21,600
Did she ask you to come back? Did she say she couldn't live here because her step-mother was so horrible,

214
00:24:21,600 --> 00:24:24,800
that she needed the Granny and Auntie who raised her like their own?

215
00:24:24,800 --> 00:24:26,800
Did she hold on to you?

216
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:30,430
This is a big deal. You've got a lot of misunderstandings,

217
00:24:30,430 --> 00:24:32,600
that's making a big deal out of this situation.

218
00:24:32,600 --> 00:24:36,000
Madam, please ask Big Miss.

219
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:38,400
Because Big Miss asked us to stay here...

220
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:41,000
Oh, Grandma! The people who work are so hungry!

221
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:43,700
Why aren't you feeding us when it's already past lunch time...?

222
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:54,400
You still haven't left Hyo Seon's Uncle?

223
00:24:54,400 --> 00:24:57,300
The thing is that...

224
00:24:58,600 --> 00:25:01,600
Mom, please.

225
00:25:01,600 --> 00:25:05,800
If Uncle is kicked out of here, he really has nowhere else to go, Mom.

226
00:25:08,400 --> 00:25:11,200
Look here, Hyo Seon's Uncle.

227
00:25:11,200 --> 00:25:16,000
You can't do this. Who's fault is it that this household is in this mess?

228
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:19,100
Whose fault is it that our Joon Soo's dad left like that so abruptly?!

229
00:25:19,100 --> 00:25:21,800
How? With what nerve? With what conscience?

230
00:25:21,800 --> 00:25:25,500
Are you coming into and leaving my house!

231
00:25:26,800 --> 00:25:28,400
Mom..

232
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:31,800
Hey talk to me if you have a mouth! Are you an idiot?!

233
00:25:31,800 --> 00:25:34,000
You still don't know what make your dad be gone?

234
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:36,600
If only your Uncle hadn't caused all this trouble-

235
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:38,400
Mom!

236
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:09,170
Let go of me, you brat! Why do I have

237
00:26:09,170 --> 00:26:11,400
to be dragged into my own house, you brat?!

238
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:13,400
Let go of me.

239
00:26:24,400 --> 00:26:28,400
Why are you looking at me with such brazen eyes, looking to talk haughtily to me?!

240
00:26:28,400 --> 00:26:29,800
Did I say something wrong?

241
00:26:29,800 --> 00:26:33,100
Who are you to call back all the people I chased out?

242
00:26:33,120 --> 00:26:37,790
Mom... Mom, you're on my side, right?

243
00:26:37,810 --> 00:26:40,500
- You're not on Hyo Seon's side, right?
- What?

244
00:26:40,500 --> 00:26:43,380
If we add your share, mine and Jun Soo's together,

245
00:26:43,380 --> 00:26:46,300
it will be three and a half times as much as Hyo Seon's?

246
00:26:48,200 --> 00:26:52,800
Does Hyo Seon have to get that much?

247
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:57,400
Hyo Seon ... she's just an idiot,

248
00:26:57,400 --> 00:27:02,000
if you act all nice to her, we can get it all.

249
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:07,670
She's an idiot. She says that she'd rather have a nagging mom like you

250
00:27:07,670 --> 00:27:10,600
than not have a mom at all.

251
00:27:11,700 --> 00:27:16,200
Do you think I'm telling you to be kind to her because I can't handle an idiot like her?

252
00:27:16,200 --> 00:27:18,600
What you're doing to Hyo Seon,

253
00:27:18,600 --> 00:27:22,400
chasing out her Uncle and the kitchen staff.

254
00:27:22,400 --> 00:27:25,400
All the workers and elders of the house found out about that.

255
00:27:25,400 --> 00:27:28,200
Once the elders of the household start talking,

256
00:27:28,200 --> 00:27:32,000
everything that you and I can take shrinks.

257
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:34,400
What kind of bullshit is that?

258
00:27:34,400 --> 00:27:37,000
What do the elders have to do with this household?

259
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:40,800
Dae Seong True Wine Makers is no longer ours, Mom.

260
00:27:41,600 --> 00:27:44,200
Since we couldn't pay back the money the elders loaned us,

261
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:47,800
we gave the elders shares to Dae Seong True Winemakers.

262
00:27:47,800 --> 00:27:49,200
When?!

263
00:27:49,200 --> 00:27:51,200
Do you think that's all?

264
00:27:51,200 --> 00:27:54,060
When you go against Hyo Seon and the workers,

265
00:27:54,060 --> 00:27:56,600
all the elders who have shares will take Hyo Seon's side.

266
00:27:56,600 --> 00:28:00,200
It's a matter of time before our shares hit rock bottom.

267
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:04,400
The ancestral mountain and 200000 plots of farmland...

268
00:28:04,400 --> 00:28:09,200
All that, too, is jointly owned by those people.

269
00:28:09,200 --> 00:28:13,600
Don't you think we need to get that too?

270
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:20,200
If we want to sell the land, but Hyo Seon disagrees, then we can't sell it.

271
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:22,600
Really?

272
00:28:22,600 --> 00:28:25,000
Stop being mean to Hyo Seon.

273
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:29,800
Since you're acting this way, it makes me want to treat Hyo Seon super well.

274
00:28:29,800 --> 00:28:34,400
But like you said, I can't put on that kind of act.

275
00:28:34,400 --> 00:28:37,900
That's why you need to treat her well in my place, okay?

276
00:28:39,800 --> 00:28:42,100
Do you not understand what I'm saying?

277
00:28:42,100 --> 00:28:47,000
I'm saying there's a lot you can take from Hyo Seon.

278
00:29:09,200 --> 00:29:11,000
Noona.

279
00:29:25,600 --> 00:29:29,500
Let's go to the hospital. We have to get you examined first,

280
00:29:33,200 --> 00:29:35,300
It's not that sort of thing.

281
00:29:36,350 --> 00:29:38,470
It's not that sort of thing.

282
00:29:39,400 --> 00:29:43,500
It's just that my heart got a little stuffy..

283
00:30:04,990 --> 00:30:07,430
She told me not to cry.

284
00:30:08,990 --> 00:30:11,260
Eun Jo did.

285
00:30:14,330 --> 00:30:18,330
She must not like it when people cry.

286
00:30:22,010 --> 00:30:24,060
It's okay.

287
00:30:24,900 --> 00:30:29,500
Still... I'm not clinging on anymore.

288
00:30:31,200 --> 00:30:34,200
There are times when she's friendly.

289
00:30:39,150 --> 00:30:41,270
But still...

290
00:30:43,500 --> 00:30:46,400
I feel so overwhelmed, Oppa.

291
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:57,200
Why do you think I was born like this, Oppa?

292
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:09,300
I miss Dad so much, Oppa..

293
00:31:13,600 --> 00:31:17,600
I miss him so much that I could die.

294
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:24,100
You can't cry because Eun Jo told you not to cry?

295
00:31:25,800 --> 00:31:31,300
Cry. You feel overwhelmed because you can't cry.

296
00:31:35,400 --> 00:31:38,700
Cry. You're in front of me now.

297
00:31:41,400 --> 00:31:43,400
Can I do that?

298
00:31:44,800 --> 00:31:46,400
Yes.

299
00:32:03,800 --> 00:32:05,900
You can cry aloud.

300
00:32:23,200 --> 00:32:27,200
I'm sorry ... sorry,

301
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:33,100
I'm sorry.

302
00:32:35,150 --> 00:32:37,570
I'm sorry, Hyo Seon.

303
00:32:58,510 --> 00:33:02,020
Nurungji Makgeolli, 1,500 won.

304
00:33:02,030 --> 00:33:04,730
Place of Production, Nurungji Winery..

305
00:33:05,800 --> 00:33:09,400
You're not going to ask me how I've been doing while I was away?

306
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:13,400
You said you were going to the reserve forces training. I'm sure you've been well.

307
00:33:14,700 --> 00:33:17,000
Bok Boon Da Makgeolli, 1,800 won.

308
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:21,300
Place of Production, Dong Shin. Type is aged makgeolli.

309
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:27,000
You're still wearing the bread (brooch), right?

310
00:33:30,600 --> 00:33:33,700
Bread. I'm asking if you still wear the bread!

311
00:33:33,760 --> 00:33:36,000
Soo Da Makgeolli, 1,700 won.

312
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:39,690
Place of Production, Soo Da Makgeolli.

313
00:33:47,400 --> 00:33:50,600
Jo Won Soo Makgeolli, 1,800 won.

314
00:33:50,600 --> 00:33:54,300
If you need any help, let me know.

315
00:33:56,140 --> 00:34:01,240
How much money could you possibly have that you always offer me some?

316
00:34:09,400 --> 00:34:10,800
It's yours.

317
00:34:10,800 --> 00:34:12,300
What's this?

318
00:34:12,300 --> 00:34:14,600
I won it playing "Go Stop".

319
00:34:14,600 --> 00:34:16,000
What?

320
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:18,400
It's nothing. I was just kidding.

321
00:34:25,200 --> 00:34:28,000
You..aren't you going to eat?

322
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:32,900
Your face looks so thin and pale. Get up immediately.

323
00:34:34,200 --> 00:34:36,800
What are you doing?! I have a mountain load of work to do!!

324
00:34:36,800 --> 00:34:39,000
I'm just telling you to eat while you work!

325
00:34:40,180 --> 00:34:43,950
Do you want to fool around? I told you to not fool around!!

326
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:47,500
- You shouldn't fool around either.
- What?

327
00:34:47,500 --> 00:34:52,800
I don't know about anything else, but I won't let you not eat.

328
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:54,800
Follow me.

329
00:35:30,600 --> 00:35:32,200
Come on.

330
00:35:34,600 --> 00:35:36,300
Welcome.

331
00:35:59,600 --> 00:36:01,400
Unni.

332
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:21,200
What kind of relationship do you two have?

333
00:36:21,200 --> 00:36:23,600
What relationship?

334
00:36:26,400 --> 00:36:32,600
"Song Eun Jo is Han Jeong Woo's woman forever." What was that bat about?

335
00:36:32,600 --> 00:36:34,600
Ah, that's...

336
00:36:35,400 --> 00:36:38,600
If you finished eating your meal, let's go.

337
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:43,200
No. Why aren't you finishing your rice? It's rice after all.

338
00:36:43,800 --> 00:36:47,500
You and I... we can't leave any leftovers.

339
00:37:03,000 --> 00:37:04,800
Hyo Seon, eat.

340
00:37:12,700 --> 00:37:17,600
Eat lots. Why are you so thin?

341
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:43,300
Hyo Seon is back.

342
00:37:45,400 --> 00:37:47,600
You're back, Hyo Seon?

343
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:50,800
Did you eat dinner already?

344
00:37:50,800 --> 00:37:52,400
We did.

345
00:37:52,400 --> 00:37:55,400
Ah, is that so? Then, you should wash up and go to bed.

346
00:38:09,720 --> 00:38:11,540
Just go to sleep.

347
00:38:12,400 --> 00:38:15,400
I should say "hi" to Mom.

348
00:38:15,400 --> 00:38:19,300
You already did. Just sleep.

349
00:39:01,600 --> 00:39:05,700
Are you this happy because Mom isn't getting angry at you?

350
00:39:05,700 --> 00:39:07,400
Is it obvious?

351
00:39:09,760 --> 00:39:12,990
It makes me a little nervous...

352
00:39:16,400 --> 00:39:19,200
It makes me a little nervous.

353
00:39:20,170 --> 00:39:22,390
But, I'm happy.

354
00:40:40,600 --> 00:40:43,300
This is the only one that's just right.

355
00:40:43,300 --> 00:40:44,600
What did you say?

356
00:40:44,600 --> 00:40:47,600
The rest of the drinks taste different.

357
00:40:47,600 --> 00:40:51,600
How is it different? We made them all the same!

358
00:40:51,600 --> 00:40:55,800
It means the yeast made all different tastes.

359
00:40:55,800 --> 00:41:00,300
It's okay. Anyway, we've still succeeded.

360
00:41:00,300 --> 00:41:06,360
We can just research what needs to be come to make the yeast all taste the same.

361
00:41:21,860 --> 00:41:23,980
The makgeolli made of nature. Dae Seong True Winemakers Makgeolli.

362
00:41:36,830 --> 00:41:39,430
The makgeolli made of nature. Dae Seong True Wineakers Makgeolli.

363
00:41:52,800 --> 00:41:56,600
Miss Mi Yoo Ra has rescinded the contract.

364
00:41:56,600 --> 00:42:01,200
To be precise, she refuses to stamp the contract.

365
00:42:01,200 --> 00:42:02,400
What are you talking about?

366
00:42:02,400 --> 00:42:04,400
She said there's a problem with the quality of the makgeolli.

367
00:42:04,400 --> 00:42:05,800
What problem?

368
00:42:05,800 --> 00:42:09,200
Instead of saying that there's a problem with Hong Joo Ga's makgeolli,

369
00:42:09,200 --> 00:42:13,200
she says that she's decided to go for a better quality product.

370
00:42:13,200 --> 00:42:16,000
A better quality product?

371
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:19,500
Last time, Dae Seong True Wineamakers ...

372
00:42:22,000 --> 00:42:28,660
Half of what was in the container was unloaded and marketed in Japan.

373
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:34,100
- The reception...
- What about the reception?

374
00:42:34,100 --> 00:42:37,500
was great.

375
00:42:39,800 --> 00:42:42,200
Great?

376
00:42:42,830 --> 00:42:46,430
Amongst the youngsters in Japan, it's a trend to search up information

377
00:42:46,430 --> 00:42:50,900
about Dae Sung True Winemakers before their friends.

378
00:42:50,900 --> 00:42:54,600
They say the commercial video for Dae Seong True Winemakers,

379
00:42:54,600 --> 00:42:58,000
as well as their advertisement pages

380
00:42:58,000 --> 00:43:01,200
are circulating all over.

381
00:43:01,200 --> 00:43:05,400
So much that it can be seen as a strange fandom phenomenon.

382
00:43:05,400 --> 00:43:10,100
Didn't you report that the yeast was not completely successful?

383
00:43:11,000 --> 00:43:14,200
The ingredient prepared by the late owner was all used up

384
00:43:14,200 --> 00:43:17,310
and the 2nd generation is not capable enough to prepare it,

385
00:43:17,310 --> 00:43:21,400
isn't that what you reported?

386
00:43:21,400 --> 00:43:26,400
So, how is it possible that Dae Seong True Winemakers has been able to receive new orders?

387
00:43:26,400 --> 00:43:32,000
Gi Hoon is said to have negotiated with Mr. Miura.

388
00:43:32,000 --> 00:43:35,000
He asked to borrow the latest technology

389
00:43:35,000 --> 00:43:39,000
and equipment to complete the unfinished yeast development.

390
00:43:39,000 --> 00:43:44,000
Mr. Miura is positively reviewing the request.

391
00:43:48,450 --> 00:43:54,080
Until that came to pass, what have you been doing?

392
00:43:55,600 --> 00:43:57,800
What were you doing?!

393
00:44:01,300 --> 00:44:06,000
Yes. Yes, thank you very much. (In Japanese)

394
00:44:06,000 --> 00:44:11,200
We'll try to come to a decision quickly and let you know as soon as possible.

395
00:44:20,200 --> 00:44:21,800
Let's do it.

396
00:44:21,800 --> 00:44:26,400
Let's lease the machinery. Your yeast was not a failure.

397
00:44:26,400 --> 00:44:30,100
All we need to do is figure out the conditions in which the yeast will produce the right taste.

398
00:44:30,100 --> 00:44:31,600
Let's do it.

399
00:44:31,600 --> 00:44:35,600
An opportunity like this is once in a lifetime.

400
00:44:36,710 --> 00:44:40,400
Eun Jo, are you listening?

401
00:44:41,800 --> 00:44:44,000
Eun Jo.

402
00:44:44,000 --> 00:44:49,200
What if we fail again?

403
00:44:49,200 --> 00:44:50,400
Eun Jo.

404
00:44:50,400 --> 00:44:56,800
What if... we fall into debt again?

405
00:44:56,800 --> 00:44:59,400
That won't happen.

406
00:44:59,400 --> 00:45:03,000
Those people are businessmen to their core.

407
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:06,600
Would they offer us something like this without confidence that we would succeed?

408
00:45:06,600 --> 00:45:10,700
Believe in yourself. I said believe in yourself.

409
00:45:13,600 --> 00:45:16,000
This all happened

410
00:45:17,230 --> 00:45:19,610
because I believed in myself.

411
00:45:20,540 --> 00:45:25,400
At least you can ask Ajhusshi for forgiveness like this.

412
00:45:26,560 --> 00:45:28,640
I don't have anything.

413
00:45:32,010 --> 00:45:34,340
I'm jealous that you have a way.

414
00:45:38,400 --> 00:45:42,400
He'll like it. Ahjussi will.

415
00:46:26,600 --> 00:46:28,600
Don't do this.

416
00:46:32,420 --> 00:46:34,010
This...

417
00:46:36,400 --> 00:46:38,400
Please don't do it.

418
00:46:57,600 --> 00:46:59,900
We have to give them an answer quickly.

419
00:47:00,710 --> 00:47:03,100
You've made up your mind, right?

420
00:47:05,600 --> 00:47:07,800
The costs are too high.

421
00:47:07,800 --> 00:47:12,800
Even if we get orders, it'll basically be the same as giving out our first batch for free.

422
00:47:12,800 --> 00:47:16,800
We'll have to take at least that much risk. You know that.

423
00:47:16,800 --> 00:47:21,000
On top of that, we can't trust them.

424
00:47:21,000 --> 00:47:24,600
What if we get tricked like last time?

425
00:47:24,600 --> 00:47:27,200
This... isn't like that.

426
00:47:28,800 --> 00:47:31,600
Why didn't I do anything?

427
00:47:33,200 --> 00:47:35,600
Who did that...

428
00:47:35,600 --> 00:47:38,600
Why they did that...

429
00:47:38,600 --> 00:47:42,800
Why didn't I think of trying to find that out? Why did I stay still?

430
00:47:42,800 --> 00:47:44,300
Eun Jo.

431
00:47:45,980 --> 00:47:51,210
I'm going to find out. No matter what it takes, I'm going to catch them somehow.

432
00:48:00,200 --> 00:48:01,400
What?

433
00:48:01,400 --> 00:48:02,600
I'll do it.

434
00:48:02,600 --> 00:48:06,400
I'll find out. It'll be better if I do it.

435
00:48:06,400 --> 00:48:09,200
No, I'm going to do it.

436
00:48:10,000 --> 00:48:12,200
I'll do it.

437
00:48:12,200 --> 00:48:16,000
Eventually, I'll tell you why it is that I have to find out.

438
00:48:16,000 --> 00:48:17,000
What do you mean?

439
00:48:17,000 --> 00:48:23,000
Make the yeast samples quickly. Make a lot of them.

440
00:48:23,000 --> 00:48:27,600
Prepare it so that we can export them to Japan as soon as possible.

441
00:48:27,600 --> 00:48:30,800
If we succeed, ideally in 1-2 months, if it takes longer, at least within 6 months.

442
00:48:30,800 --> 00:48:36,200
Dae Seong True Winemakers can rise again. If that happens,

443
00:48:41,900 --> 00:48:45,800
Get in. I'll take you to the research lab.

444
00:48:54,000 --> 00:48:57,400
"Dae Seong True Winemakers' Meaningful Movement"
"We Pride Ourselves on Making the Purest Makgeolli"

445
00:48:59,810 --> 00:49:03,150
Please raise your face a little bit higher.

446
00:49:08,400 --> 00:49:12,100
Okay, we're done. Finish it now...

447
00:49:15,800 --> 00:49:21,000
But, why was I being photographed, Dong Soo?

448
00:49:21,000 --> 00:49:25,600
On the back cover, we featured a reader reading our magazine.

449
00:49:25,600 --> 00:49:28,200
You're the next issue's cover.

450
00:49:55,600 --> 00:49:59,300
You can leave now. There's no reason for you to stay here.

451
00:50:01,500 --> 00:50:03,500
If...

452
00:50:04,800 --> 00:50:09,500
Last time's Japanese export incident...

453
00:50:09,500 --> 00:50:13,400
Who did that, why they did it.

454
00:50:13,400 --> 00:50:15,800
If we find out everything,

455
00:50:18,400 --> 00:50:21,000
what are you going to do with those people?

456
00:50:21,800 --> 00:50:23,600
I don't know.

457
00:50:24,840 --> 00:50:30,010
I'll find the strength to live for something for the rest of my life.

458
00:50:31,000 --> 00:50:34,600
I'm sure I'll overflow with energy

459
00:50:34,600 --> 00:50:37,600
thinking of their faces and hating them with all my might.

460
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:42,800
I'll hate them without getting tired of hating them.

461
00:50:42,850 --> 00:50:46,100
That'll be enough for me.

462
00:50:46,150 --> 00:50:53,510
With the strength to hate them, I'll live well until I die.

463
00:50:56,400 --> 00:50:58,400
You can go.

464
00:52:08,000 --> 00:52:09,700
What?

465
00:52:12,370 --> 00:52:13,950
What is it?

466
00:52:15,300 --> 00:52:17,200
What are you doing right now?

467
00:52:17,230 --> 00:52:19,490
My friend and I run a business together.

468
00:52:19,490 --> 00:52:22,810
- It hasn't been long since we started.
- What?

469
00:52:22,820 --> 00:52:25,800
Look around. When production begins,

470
00:52:25,830 --> 00:52:29,770
You can supply us with Dae Seong True Winemakers makgeolli here.

471
00:52:29,800 --> 00:52:32,000
- What?
- It'll be all right.

472
00:52:32,000 --> 00:52:36,200
It hasn't been long since we opened it, but there are so many customers.

473
00:52:37,600 --> 00:52:42,400
You aren't a reporter? I thought you were a reporter.

474
00:52:42,400 --> 00:52:44,200
Haven't you heard of having two jobs?

475
00:52:48,200 --> 00:52:49,800
Aren't you going to leave?

476
00:52:49,800 --> 00:52:52,600
I'm done talking. Leave quickly.

477
00:52:57,500 --> 00:53:01,100
What's wrong with me meeting that kid?

478
00:53:01,100 --> 00:53:03,800
What is father trying to meet her for?

479
00:53:03,800 --> 00:53:06,200
You don't need to know that.

480
00:53:06,200 --> 00:53:08,000
What are you up to?

481
00:53:08,000 --> 00:53:09,800
Stop interfering now.

482
00:53:09,800 --> 00:53:12,400
I told you to leave this place as it is!

483
00:53:16,800 --> 00:53:20,400
Do you have the right to say that?

484
00:53:20,400 --> 00:53:23,000
Leave it?

485
00:53:23,000 --> 00:53:26,900
Did you go into Dae Sung True Winemakers to leave it be?

486
00:53:28,000 --> 00:53:32,300
If you meet with Eun Jo, what are you going to say?

487
00:53:33,000 --> 00:53:36,800
I'd like to tell her a bit about what you did.

488
00:53:37,600 --> 00:53:38,800
What did you say?

489
00:53:38,800 --> 00:53:40,800
If I do that,

490
00:53:40,800 --> 00:53:46,200
then I'll have to tell her what I did as well. But, I don't care.

491
00:53:51,500 --> 00:53:54,600
Anyway, I'm going to lose everything.

492
00:53:56,600 --> 00:54:00,000
Gi Jeong's mother is planning on filing for a divorce.

493
00:54:01,200 --> 00:54:05,600
I'm supposed to hand over my shares as alimony.

494
00:54:06,700 --> 00:54:09,600
If my shares go to Gi Jeong's mom...

495
00:54:09,600 --> 00:54:13,800
In other words, that means they'll be Gi Jeong's.

496
00:54:13,800 --> 00:54:18,000
Then, Hong Joo Ga will belong to Gi Jeong.

497
00:54:22,100 --> 00:54:25,200
Since I'm about to lose everything anyway...

498
00:54:25,200 --> 00:54:28,500
I came to confess all my sins.

499
00:54:30,400 --> 00:54:32,000
Father.

500
00:54:32,700 --> 00:54:36,400
What? Can't I do that?

501
00:54:36,400 --> 00:54:38,200
Don't do this.

502
00:54:38,200 --> 00:54:41,000
Don't do anything!

503
00:54:44,000 --> 00:54:47,000
I heard you got some good news from Japan.

504
00:54:48,570 --> 00:54:50,920
I heard that it was your doing.

505
00:54:53,700 --> 00:54:57,200
If you don't want me to meet that child Eun Jo,

506
00:54:57,200 --> 00:54:59,500
you better be on my side.

507
00:55:05,600 --> 00:55:10,200
If you succeed, within 1-2 months at the earliest and within 6 months at the latest

508
00:55:10,200 --> 00:55:13,400
Dae Sung True Winemakers can rise again.

509
00:55:35,150 --> 00:55:37,440
Who are you?

510
00:55:49,050 --> 00:55:54,420
Hand over Dae Seong True Winemakers which is appreciating in value.

511
00:55:54,460 --> 00:55:57,940
Then, I will finish raising it.

512
00:55:57,960 --> 00:56:02,890
That is the only way I can stay at Hong Distillery.

513
00:56:04,000 --> 00:56:05,800
I refuse.

514
00:56:05,800 --> 00:56:10,980
Then, I'll have no other choice. I'll have to meet that child named Eun Jo.

515
00:56:17,980 --> 00:56:22,350
When will we be able to use the machine?

516
00:56:22,370 --> 00:56:24,350
What?

517
00:56:24,350 --> 00:56:29,320
You said to rent them. Let's do it.

518
00:56:30,390 --> 00:56:32,020
Okay.

519
00:56:33,250 --> 00:56:40,520
Let me do it as soon as possible. I can make at least a sample whenever we need.

520
00:56:45,800 --> 00:56:47,400
Okay.

521
00:56:53,800 --> 00:56:55,700
Eun Jo.

522
00:57:07,960 --> 00:57:11,420
Never mind. All right.

523
00:57:31,400 --> 00:57:33,600
Are you coming back home now?

524
00:57:35,200 --> 00:57:41,000
She told us to come back to the house all of a sudden. Madam did that.

525
00:57:41,800 --> 00:57:45,200
I see. What about Ahjumma?

526
00:57:46,200 --> 00:57:48,400
I came too.

527
00:57:56,600 --> 00:58:00,000
Seriously telling us to believe that, right?

528
00:58:39,600 --> 00:58:41,800
This is funny, isn't it?

529
00:58:42,600 --> 00:58:44,800
Joon Soo, you should go to sleep now.

530
00:58:44,800 --> 00:58:46,400
I don't want to.

531
00:58:46,400 --> 00:58:47,900
Go to sleep immediately!

532
00:58:59,600 --> 00:59:01,400
Aren't you going to sleep?

533
00:59:04,200 --> 00:59:06,600
I just want to watch this.

534
00:59:09,600 --> 00:59:12,800
- Ah, right. Mom.
- What?

535
00:59:14,600 --> 00:59:18,000
Jang... Who was it?

536
00:59:18,000 --> 00:59:21,000
Jang... Jang...

537
00:59:21,800 --> 00:59:25,200
Do you know a man named Jang Taek Geun?

538
00:59:27,200 --> 00:59:28,800
Who?

539
00:59:29,800 --> 00:59:32,000
Do you or don't you?

540
00:59:32,800 --> 00:59:36,000
I don't. Why?

541
00:59:36,000 --> 00:59:40,500
You don't? Then forget it.

542
00:59:41,400 --> 00:59:44,600
Earlier, while I was coming back home there was this kind of man that I saw...

543
00:59:49,800 --> 00:59:52,400
What kind of man was that?

544
01:00:01,000 --> 01:00:03,500
Mom, what is it?

545
01:00:04,400 --> 01:00:06,400
It's funny.

546
01:00:06,400 --> 01:00:08,600
What kind of man was that?

547
01:00:08,620 --> 01:00:16,200
Oh, that kind of man asked if this is the house

548
01:00:16,200 --> 01:00:20,160
where Jang Taek Geun's Noona, Song Kang Sook, lives.

549
01:00:21,200 --> 01:00:24,560
So I told him that I know that my mom doesn't have any relatives

550
01:00:24,560 --> 01:00:27,450
and that he got the wrong house.

551
01:00:29,200 --> 01:00:32,700
You did well. I don't have any relatives.

552
01:00:36,300 --> 01:00:39,700
Go on and sleep. I'm tired.

553
01:00:41,800 --> 01:00:45,800
Okay. Sleep well.

554
01:00:45,800 --> 01:00:48,000
All right, you sleep well too.

555
01:00:57,680 --> 01:01:05,360
Mom, I know that you don't find me lovable.

556
01:01:06,730 --> 01:01:13,440
But thank you for being kind to me regardless.

557
01:01:14,790 --> 01:01:20,960
Later on, I really want you to give me a hug because you find me loveable.

558
01:01:22,620 --> 01:01:25,650
I'll be good to you, Mom.

559
01:01:46,400 --> 01:01:49,600
Who did it and why...

560
01:01:49,600 --> 01:01:53,600
If we find out everything, what are you going to
do with those people?

561
01:01:53,600 --> 01:01:58,400
I'll find the strength to live forever.

562
01:01:58,400 --> 01:02:04,800
I'll overflow with strength thinking of their faces and hating them.

563
01:02:04,800 --> 01:02:10,400
With the strength to despise those people, I'll live well until I die.

564
01:02:28,200 --> 01:02:29,200
What?

565
01:02:29,200 --> 01:02:34,400
Before you tell her, I'm going to confess first and end this.

566
01:02:34,400 --> 01:02:38,800
If I tell her first, you'll be the only one who'll be ruined.

567
01:02:38,800 --> 01:02:43,800
Unburdened, I can simply wait for her disposition.

568
01:02:43,830 --> 01:02:52,680
I didn't know that was the best way of never letting you or hyung get your hands on Dae Seong True Winemakers.

569
01:02:53,800 --> 01:02:56,300
Good night.

570
01:02:58,310 --> 01:03:00,180
Father...

571
01:03:03,100 --> 01:03:05,400
I'm going to Eun Jo now.

572
01:03:09,090 --> 01:03:14,800
Father, you're done for.

573
01:04:05,400 --> 01:04:10,000
Open the door. Open the door!

574
01:04:11,100 --> 01:04:13,400
Open the door, Eun Jo.

575
01:04:13,400 --> 01:04:18,000
Open the door. Eun Jo, open the door!

576
01:04:18,000 --> 01:04:21,800
Eun Jo! Eun Jo!

577
01:04:22,790 --> 01:04:25,480
Eun Jo!

578
01:04:25,490 --> 01:04:29,550
♫  It must be you  ♫

579
01:04:29,590 --> 01:04:33,000
♫  I cannot be without you  ♫

580
01:04:33,000 --> 01:04:39,800
♫  Like this for another day, month or year  ♫

581
01:04:39,820 --> 01:04:43,730
♫  I don't mind even if I am hurt  ♫

582
01:04:43,740 --> 01:04:47,570
♫  I don't mind even if my heart breaks  ♫

583
01:04:47,590 --> 01:04:53,600
♫  because, yes, you are the only one I love  ♫

584
01:04:53,600 --> 01:04:57,200
♫  My bruised heart  ♫

585
01:04:57,200 --> 01:05:01,110
♫  is shouting so that  ♫

586
01:05:01,110 --> 01:05:06,000
♫  I can find you  ♫

587
01:05:06,000 --> 01:05:09,650
♫  Wherever you are  ♫

588
01:05:09,670 --> 01:05:12,510
♫  Can't you hear my voice?  ♫
